WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.087 --> 00:00:04.453
The kids were outside doing chores.

2
00:00:04.454 --> 00:00:08.238
The boys were feeding the goats and chickens.

3
00:00:08.239 --> 00:00:11.527
Izzie was picking tomatoes.

4
00:00:11.528 --> 00:00:16.339
Nina's job was to cut basil in the herb garden.

5
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.006
The names of the herbs were printed on wooden signs.

6
00:00:20.007 --> 00:00:23.554
Nina pulled them out of the soil.

7
00:00:23.555 --> 00:00:25.809
"Izzie, look!

8
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:32.248
These cute signs look like they belong to fairies."

9
00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:36.455
Izzie giggled.

10
00:00:36.456 --> 00:00:40.557
"Maybe fairies are in this garden!"

11
00:00:40.558 --> 00:00:46.569
The girls stuck the signs in hidden places where fairies might live.

12
00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:48.874
The boys walked over.

13
00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:52.950
"We're going inside," Bobby said.

14
00:00:52.951 --> 00:00:58.106
"You should come in soon too or Chef will get mad."

15
00:00:58.107 --> 00:01:01.642
The girls collected the signs.

16
00:01:01.643 --> 00:01:04.719
But Nina couldn't remember where they went.

17
00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.143
"Uh-oh," she said nervously.

18
00:01:08.144 --> 00:01:11.204
"Which herb is basil?"

19
00:01:11.205 --> 00:01:15.624
Izzie shrugged. "I don't know."

20
00:01:15.625 --> 00:01:21.458
Nina gulped. "I'll just cut a bunch of herbs.

21
00:01:21.459 --> 00:01:26.318
Hopefully, one will be basil."

22
00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.528
The girls rushed inside.

23
00:01:29.529 --> 00:01:33.612
Nina put the basket on the counter.

24
00:01:33.613 --> 00:01:37.664
Chef frowned. "What's this?

25
00:01:37.665 --> 00:01:42.876
I asked for basil! Why did you bring all these?"

26
00:01:42.877 --> 00:01:48.847
"Uh . . . we . . ." Izzie tried to explain.

27
00:01:48.848 --> 00:01:52.980
"I'm sorry! I mixed up the signs."

28
00:01:52.981 --> 00:01:55.275
Nina hung her head.

29
00:01:55.276 --> 00:01:59.685
"Now you won't know which herbs are which."

30
00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.813
Chef laughed.

31
00:02:02.814 --> 00:02:06.490
"Nonsense! I know all the herbs in my garden.

32
00:02:06.491 --> 00:02:11.320
You can learn to identify them too."

33
00:02:11.321 --> 00:02:14.283
He washed the herbs.

34
00:02:14.284 --> 00:02:18.354
Then he set them out in four separate bowls.

35
00:02:18.355 --> 00:02:23.366
"You can identify herbs by the way they look, smell, and taste.

36
00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:26.887
Bobby, take one of these herbs and describe it."

37
00:02:26.888 --> 00:02:31.909
Bobby picked up some long, green strands.

38
00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:36.993
"This herb looks like grass and smells like onions."

39
00:02:36.994 --> 00:02:40.762
"Those are chives," Chef said.

40
00:02:40.763 --> 00:02:44.178
"We use them as a garnish for many dishes.

41
00:02:44.179 --> 00:02:47.315
Now it's Nina's turn."

42
00:02:47.316 --> 00:02:50.482
Nina's herb had shiny, green leaves.

43
00:02:50.483 --> 00:02:55.572
"It smells like . . . pizza!"

44
00:02:55.573 --> 00:03:00.544
"That's the basil we'll use today to make pesto," Chef said.

45
00:03:00.545 --> 00:03:03.557
"We're going to spread it on sandwiches.

46
00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:07.743
It's used in many Italian dishes too."

47
00:03:07.744 --> 00:03:12.005
"Jason and I have the same herb," Izzie said.

48
00:03:12.006 --> 00:03:16.056
Their herb had lots of small leaves.

49
00:03:16.057 --> 00:03:19.977
"They look alike, but your herbs taste very different.

50
00:03:19.978 --> 00:03:24.871
Try them," Chef said.

51
00:03:24.872 --> 00:03:29.988
"Mine tastes green and peppery," Izzie said.

52
00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:33.444
"That's parsley," Chef said.

53
00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:36.014
Jason nibbled his herb.

54
00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.480
"It has a soapy taste."

55
00:03:39.481 --> 00:03:44.887
"It's cilantro, which is used in Mexican and Asian dishes.

56
00:03:44.888 --> 00:03:47.561
These are just four herbs.

57
00:03:47.562 --> 00:03:51.498
You'll get to know them better as you cook more."

58
00:03:51.499 --> 00:03:54.446
It was time to make pesto.

59
00:03:54.447 --> 00:03:58.188
Nina dumped the basil into the food processor.

60
00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:02.077
Izzie peeled two garlic cloves and added those.

61
00:04:02.078 --> 00:04:05.503
Jason poured in pine nuts.

62
00:04:05.504 --> 00:04:08.512
Bobby turned on the processor.

63
00:04:08.513 --> 00:04:11.820
It whirred as everything mixed together.

64
00:04:11.821 --> 00:04:16.952
Chef slowly poured in half a cup of olive oil.

65
00:04:16.953 --> 00:04:19.241
He turned off the machine.

66
00:04:19.242 --> 00:04:23.828
"Yum! Smell that basil!"

67
00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:28.994
Jason grated Parmesan cheese and added it to the mixture.

68
00:04:28.995 --> 00:04:35.499
Bobby turned on the processor again.

69
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.910
"My favorite color!" Izzie said.

70
00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:42.812
"It's bright green and smooth!"

71
00:04:42.813 --> 00:04:47.063
Jason spread pesto on slices of bread.

72
00:04:47.064 --> 00:04:51.920
Izzie sliced the tomatoes, and Nina cut up mozzarella cheese.

73
00:04:51.921 --> 00:04:57.219
Bobby put the sandwiches together.

74
00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.233
Nina took a bite.

75
00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:02.871
She loved all the different flavors.

76
00:05:02.872 --> 00:05:06.401
"Now I know what basil looks like!

77
00:05:06.402 --> 00:05:13.175
The garden fairies can't trick me ever again!"

